{"type":"message","id":"58a6b5ae","parentId":"29b6bff7","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:09:11.842Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-02-03 17:09 UTC] BLUEPRINT A/B TEST — ALPHA (Bid-Breakdown-First)\n\nYou are running Test Alpha for the Bellevue Standpipe project. Your approach: Start from the bid breakdown, route to experts, extract only what's needed.\n\nPROJECT: NYC H+H Fire Pump and Standpipe Replacement - Bellevue Hospital\nPROJECT PATH: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/\n\nSTATUS FILE: Update /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/test-status.json as you progress (update tests.alpha section).\n\nPHASE 1: Parse Bid Items ✅ DONE\n- Bid breakdown already parsed to bid-breakdown-mapped.json (95 items, 8 experts)\n\nPHASE 2: Map to Experts ✅ DONE  \n- Items mapped in bid-breakdown-mapped.json\n\nPHASE 3: Extract Targeted Docs\n- Read the Fire Protection expert file: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/experts/fire-protection/EXPERT.md\n- Focus on items 43-51 (Fire Protection scope)\n- Extract relevant PDF pages from drawings (look for FP sheets, riser diagrams)\n- Use pdftotext or similar to extract text from spec sections 21 xx xx\n\nPHASE 4: Expert Analysis\n- Using the Fire Protection expert methodology, analyze:\n  - Standpipe system (item 49)\n  - Fire pump (item 51) \n  - Sprinkler system (item 50)\n  - Piping (item 44)\n  - Valves (item 45)\n- Document quantities, specifications, and any flags/RFIs\n\nPHASE 5: Critic Review\n- Cross-check findings against bid breakdown\n- Identify any gaps or conflicts\n- Generate summary with confidence scores\n\nOUTPUT: Write findings to /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/test-alpha-results.json\n\nUpdate status file at each phase. Report back when complete with summary of findings and metrics (time, items processed, issues found)."}],"timestamp":1770138551841}}
