{"type":"message","id":"df0341e1","parentId":"febb5ac6","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:09:33.777Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I can see the project has multiple PDFs. Let me extract text from the specifications for Division 21 (Fire Suppression). The spec files look most likely to be in the Specifications PDFs. Let me try to extract relevant text from those.\n\nLet me use pdftotext to extract the fire protection specs from the spec PDFs.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01NiUFjsYv112gmWFugvEZ9E","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd \"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/Bellevue - Standpipe\" && pdftotext -layout \"11202205_Specifications_V3_Part1 (1).pdf\" - 2>/dev/null | head -200"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01PqzYEzpc9uwKeUQBjUV4CZ","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd \"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/Bellevue - Standpipe\" && pdftotext -layout \"11202205_Specifications_V3_Part2.pdf\" - 2>/dev/null | head -200"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_015J3P3iZsUShTCPGuFrBTGE","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd \"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/Bellevue - Standpipe\" && pdftotext -layout \"11202205_Specifications_V3_Part3.pdf\" - 2>/dev/null | head -200"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":8,"output":412,"cacheRead":19104,"cacheWrite":1705,"totalTokens":21229,"cost":{"input":0.00004,"output":0.0103,"cacheRead":0.009552,"cacheWrite":0.01065625,"total":0.03054825}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770138567939}}
{"type":"message","id":"c9d58859","parentId":"df0341e1","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:09:33.929Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01NiUFjsYv112gmWFugvEZ9E","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TABLE OF CONTENTS\n\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS BID AGREEMENT AND GENERAL CONDITIONS\n\nDIVISION 02 – EXISTING CONDITIONS\n02 41 19        Selective Demolition\n02 82 13        Asbestos Abatement\n\nDIVISION 03 – CONCRETE\n03 30 53        Miscellaneous Cast-in-place Concrete\n\nDIVISION 04- MASONRY BRICK, BLOCK AND STONE\n04 20 00       Unit Masonry\n\nDIVISION 05 – METAL\n05 40 00        Cold-Formed Metal Framing\n\nDIVISION 06 – WOOD, PLASTIC AND COMPOSITE PRODUCTS\n06 10 00        Rough Carpentry\n06 20 23        Interior Finish Carpentry\n\nDIVISION 07- FIRE STOPPING SMOKE SEALS\n07 21 00        Thermal Insulation\n07 84 13        Penetration Firestopping\n07 84 43        Joint Firestopping\n07 92 00        Joint Sealants\n\nDIVISION 08 - WINDOWS AND DOORS\n08 11 13         Hollow Metal Doors & Frames\n08 31 13         Access Doors and Frames\n08 34 73         Acoustical Doors and Frames\n08 71 00         Door Hardware\n\nDIVISION 09 - FINISHES\n09 22 16.23      Gypsum Board Shaft Wall Assemblies\n09 22 16         Non-structural Metal Framing\n09 24 00         Cement Plastering\n09 29 00         Gypsum Board\n09 51 23         Acoustical Tile Ceilings\n09 51 33         Metal Pan Ceilings\n09 70 50         Resinous Flooring\n09 91 23         Interior Painting\n\nDIVISION 32 – EXTERIOR\n32 39 13     Metal Bollards\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                       Table of Contents - 1\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n                                                           TABLE OF CONTENTS\n\n\nDIVISION 21 – FIRE PROTECTION\n21 05 00         General Fire Suppression Requirements\n21 05 03         Pipe and Tubes for Fire Protection\n21 05 04         Valves for Fire Suppression\n21 05 05         Hangers, Supports and Anchors for Fire Suppression\n21 05 13         Common Motor Requirements for Fire Suppression\n21 05 48         Vibration for Fire Suppression Piping and Equipment\n21 12 00         Fire Suppression Standpipes\n21 13 13         Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems\n21 30 00         Fire Pumps\n\nDIVISION 22 – PLUMBING\n22 05 00        Common Work Results for Plumbing\n22 05 23        General Duty Valves for Plumbing Piping\n22 05 29        Hangers and Supports for Plumbing Piping and Equipment\n22 05 53        Identification for Plumbing Piping and Equipment\n22 07 00        Plumbing Insulation\n22 10 00        Plumbing Piping\n22 11 00        Facility Water Distribution\n22 13 00        Facility Sanitary Sewerage\n\nDIVISION 23 – MECHANICAL\n23 05 00        General Mechanical Requirements\n23 05 01        Scope of HVAC Work\n23 05 03        Pipe and Tubes for HVAC\n23 05 14        Motor Controls\n23 05 23        General Duty Valves for HVAC\n23 05 29        Hangers and Supports for HVAC\n23 05 48        Noise and Vibration Controls for HVAC\n23 05 53        Identification for HVAC Piping and Equipment\n23 05 93        Testing, Adjusting and Balancing for HVAC\n23 07 00        HVAC Insulation\n23 09 00        Instrumentation and Control for HVAC\n23 09 23        Direct-Digital Control System for HVAC\n23 09 93        Sequence of Operations for HVAC Controls\n23 22 16        Steam and Condensate Piping Specialties\n23 31 00        HVAC Ducts and Casings\n23 33 00        Air Duct Accessories\n23 34 00        HVAC Fans\n23 37 00        Air Outlets and Inlets\n23 82 00        Convection Heating and Cooling Units\n\nDIVISION 26 - ELECTRICAL\n26 05 00      General Electrical Requirements\n26 05 19      Low-Voltage Electrical Power Conductors and Cables\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                       Table of Contents - 2\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n                                                           TABLE OF CONTENTS\n\n26 05 20          Mineral-Insulated Metal-Sheathed Cable\n26 05 26          Grounding and Bonding for Electrical Systems\n26 05 29          Hangers and Supports for Electrical Systems\n26 05 33          Raceway and Boxes for Electrical Systems\n26 05 53          Identification for Electrical Systems\n26 27 16          Electrical Cabinets and Enclosures\n26 27 26          Wiring Devices\n26 28 13          Fuses\n26 28 16.16       Enclosed Switches\n26 28 26          Enclosed Transfer Switches\n26 51 00          Interior Lighting\n\nDIVISION 28 – ELECTRONIC SAFETY AND SECURITY\n28 31 00     Fire Detection and Alarm\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                       Table of Contents - 3\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n                                                                                                        Selective Demolition\n                                                                                                                    02 41 19\n\n\n\n      SECTION 02 41 19 - SELECTIVE DEMOLITION\n\n      PART 1         - GENERAL\n\n      1.1    RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n             A.      The following documents apply to all required work for the Project: (1) the Contract Drawings, (2) the\n                     Specifications, (3) the General Conditions, (4) the Addendum and (5) the Contract (the Owner’s\n                     Standard Construction Contract).\n\n      1.2    SUMMARY\n\n             A.      Section Includes:\n                     1.      Demolition and removal of selected portions of building or structure.\n                     2.      Demolition and removal of selected site elements.\n\n      1.3    DEFINITIONS\n\n             A.      Remove: Detach items from existing construction and legally dispose of them off-site unless indicated\n                     to be removed and salvaged or removed and reinstalled.\n\n             B.      Remove and Salvage: Carefully detach from existing construction, in a manner to prevent damage, and\n                     make ready for reuse.\n\n             C.      Remove and Reinstall: Detach items from existing construction, prepare for reuse, and reinstall where\n                     indicated.\n\n             D.      Existing to Remain: Existing items of construction that are not to be permanently removed and that are\n                     not otherwise indicated to be removed, removed and salvaged, or removed and reinstalled.\n\n      1.4    MATERIALS OWNERSHIP\n\n             A.      Unless otherwise indicated, demolition waste becomes property of the Contractor.\n\n             B.      Historic items, relics, antiques, and similar objects including, but not limited to, cornerstones and their\n                     contents, commemorative plaques and tablets, and other items of interest or value to the Owner that\n                     may be uncovered during demolition remain the property of the Owner.\n                     1.      Carefully salvage in a manner to prevent damage and promptly return to the Owner.\n\n      1.5    PREINSTALLATION MEETINGS\n\n             A.      Predemolition Conference: Conduct conference at Project site.\n                     1.    Inspect and discuss the condition of construction to be selectively demolished.\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                                                                  Selective Demolition\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                                                      02 41 19 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                                         Issued for 100% Construction Documents\nProject No. 26-2112-000                                                                                           April 12, 2024\n                                                                                                      Selective Demolition\n                                                                                                                  02 41 19\n\n\n\n                     2.      Review structural load limitations of the existing structure.\n                     3.      Review and finalize selective demolition schedule and verify availability of materials,\n                             demolition personnel, equipment, and facilities needed to make progress and avoid delays.\n                     4.      Review requirements of work performed by other trades that rely on substrates exposed by\n                             selective demolition operations.\n                     5.      Review areas where existing construction is to remain and requires protection.\n\n      1.6    SUBMITTAL PROCEDURES"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":146,"aggregated":"TABLE OF CONTENTS\n\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS BID AGREEMENT AND GENERAL CONDITIONS\n\nDIVISION 02 – EXISTING CONDITIONS\n02 41 19        Selective Demolition\n02 82 13        Asbestos Abatement\n\nDIVISION 03 – CONCRETE\n03 30 53        Miscellaneous Cast-in-place Concrete\n\nDIVISION 04- MASONRY BRICK, BLOCK AND STONE\n04 20 00       Unit Masonry\n\nDIVISION 05 – METAL\n05 40 00        Cold-Formed Metal Framing\n\nDIVISION 06 – WOOD, PLASTIC AND COMPOSITE PRODUCTS\n06 10 00        Rough Carpentry\n06 20 23        Interior Finish Carpentry\n\nDIVISION 07- FIRE STOPPING SMOKE SEALS\n07 21 00        Thermal Insulation\n07 84 13        Penetration Firestopping\n07 84 43        Joint Firestopping\n07 92 00        Joint Sealants\n\nDIVISION 08 - WINDOWS AND DOORS\n08 11 13         Hollow Metal Doors & Frames\n08 31 13         Access Doors and Frames\n08 34 73         Acoustical Doors and Frames\n08 71 00         Door Hardware\n\nDIVISION 09 - FINISHES\n09 22 16.23      Gypsum Board Shaft Wall Assemblies\n09 22 16         Non-structural Metal Framing\n09 24 00         Cement Plastering\n09 29 00         Gypsum Board\n09 51 23         Acoustical Tile Ceilings\n09 51 33         Metal Pan Ceilings\n09 70 50         Resinous Flooring\n09 91 23         Interior Painting\n\nDIVISION 32 – EXTERIOR\n32 39 13     Metal Bollards\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                       Table of Contents - 1\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n                                                           TABLE OF CONTENTS\n\n\nDIVISION 21 – FIRE PROTECTION\n21 05 00         General Fire Suppression Requirements\n21 05 03         Pipe and Tubes for Fire Protection\n21 05 04         Valves for Fire Suppression\n21 05 05         Hangers, Supports and Anchors for Fire Suppression\n21 05 13         Common Motor Requirements for Fire Suppression\n21 05 48         Vibration for Fire Suppression Piping and Equipment\n21 12 00         Fire Suppression Standpipes\n21 13 13         Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems\n21 30 00         Fire Pumps\n\nDIVISION 22 – PLUMBING\n22 05 00        Common Work Results for Plumbing\n22 05 23        General Duty Valves for Plumbing Piping\n22 05 29        Hangers and Supports for Plumbing Piping and Equipment\n22 05 53        Identification for Plumbing Piping and Equipment\n22 07 00        Plumbing Insulation\n22 10 00        Plumbing Piping\n22 11 00        Facility Water Distribution\n22 13 00        Facility Sanitary Sewerage\n\nDIVISION 23 – MECHANICAL\n23 05 00        General Mechanical Requirements\n23 05 01        Scope of HVAC Work\n23 05 03        Pipe and Tubes for HVAC\n23 05 14        Motor Controls\n23 05 23        General Duty Valves for HVAC\n23 05 29        Hangers and Supports for HVAC\n23 05 48        Noise and Vibration Controls for HVAC\n23 05 53        Identification for HVAC Piping and Equipment\n23 05 93        Testing, Adjusting and Balancing for HVAC\n23 07 00        HVAC Insulation\n23 09 00        Instrumentation and Control for HVAC\n23 09 23        Direct-Digital Control System for HVAC\n23 09 93        Sequence of Operations for HVAC Controls\n23 22 16        Steam and Condensate Piping Specialties\n23 31 00        HVAC Ducts and Casings\n23 33 00        Air Duct Accessories\n23 34 00        HVAC Fans\n23 37 00        Air Outlets and Inlets\n23 82 00        Convection Heating and Cooling Units\n\nDIVISION 26 - ELECTRICAL\n26 05 00      General Electrical Requirements\n26 05 19      Low-Voltage Electrical Power Conductors and Cables\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                       Table of Contents - 2\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n                                                           TABLE OF CONTENTS\n\n26 05 20          Mineral-Insulated Metal-Sheathed Cable\n26 05 26          Grounding and Bonding for Electrical Systems\n26 05 29          Hangers and Supports for Electrical Systems\n26 05 33          Raceway and Boxes for Electrical Systems\n26 05 53          Identification for Electrical Systems\n26 27 16          Electrical Cabinets and Enclosures\n26 27 26          Wiring Devices\n26 28 13          Fuses\n26 28 16.16       Enclosed Switches\n26 28 26          Enclosed Transfer Switches\n26 51 00          Interior Lighting\n\nDIVISION 28 – ELECTRONIC SAFETY AND SECURITY\n28 31 00     Fire Detection and Alarm\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                       Table of Contents - 3\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n                                                                                                        Selective Demolition\n                                                                                                                    02 41 19\n\n\n\n      SECTION 02 41 19 - SELECTIVE DEMOLITION\n\n      PART 1         - GENERAL\n\n      1.1    RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n             A.      The following documents apply to all required work for the Project: (1) the Contract Drawings, (2) the\n                     Specifications, (3) the General Conditions, (4) the Addendum and (5) the Contract (the Owner’s\n                     Standard Construction Contract).\n\n      1.2    SUMMARY\n\n             A.      Section Includes:\n                     1.      Demolition and removal of selected portions of building or structure.\n                     2.      Demolition and removal of selected site elements.\n\n      1.3    DEFINITIONS\n\n             A.      Remove: Detach items from existing construction and legally dispose of them off-site unless indicated\n                     to be removed and salvaged or removed and reinstalled.\n\n             B.      Remove and Salvage: Carefully detach from existing construction, in a manner to prevent damage, and\n                     make ready for reuse.\n\n             C.      Remove and Reinstall: Detach items from existing construction, prepare for reuse, and reinstall where\n                     indicated.\n\n             D.      Existing to Remain: Existing items of construction that are not to be permanently removed and that are\n                     not otherwise indicated to be removed, removed and salvaged, or removed and reinstalled.\n\n      1.4    MATERIALS OWNERSHIP\n\n             A.      Unless otherwise indicated, demolition waste becomes property of the Contractor.\n\n             B.      Historic items, relics, antiques, and similar objects including, but not limited to, cornerstones and their\n                     contents, commemorative plaques and tablets, and other items of interest or value to the Owner that\n                     may be uncovered during demolition remain the property of the Owner.\n                     1.      Carefully salvage in a manner to prevent damage and promptly return to the Owner.\n\n      1.5    PREINSTALLATION MEETINGS\n\n             A.      Predemolition Conference: Conduct conference at Project site.\n                     1.    Inspect and discuss the condition of construction to be selectively demolished.\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                                                                  Selective Demolition\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                                                      02 41 19 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                                         Issued for 100% Construction Documents\nProject No. 26-2112-000                                                                                           April 12, 2024\n                                                                                                      Selective Demolition\n                                                                                                                  02 41 19\n\n\n\n                     2.      Review structural load limitations of the existing structure.\n                     3.      Review and finalize selective demolition schedule and verify availability of materials,\n                             demolition personnel, equipment, and facilities needed to make progress and avoid delays.\n                     4.      Review requirements of work performed by other trades that rely on substrates exposed by\n                             selective demolition operations.\n                     5.      Review areas where existing construction is to remain and requires protection.\n\n      1.6    SUBMITTAL PROCEDURES","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138573923}}
{"type":"message","id":"46caaea6","parentId":"c9d58859","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:09:33.976Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01PqzYEzpc9uwKeUQBjUV4CZ","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SECTION 26 27 26\n\n                                                                                      WIRING DEVICES\n\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n\n1.01      SUMMARY\n\n   A.     Section includes:\n          1.     Wall switches\n          2.     Wall dimmers\n          3.     Receptacles\n          4.     Device plates and decorative box covers\n          5.     Multioutlet assembly\n\n   B.     Related Sections:\n          1.     Section 26 05 33 - Raceway and Boxes for Electrical Systems: Outlet boxes for wiring devices.\n\n1.02      REFERENCES\n          1.   NEMA WD 1 - General Requirements for Wiring Devices.\n          2.   NEMA WD 6 - Wiring Devices-Dimensional Requirements.\n\n1.03      SUBMITTALS\n\n   A.     Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures: Submittal\n          procedures.\n\n   B.     Product Data: Submit manufacturer's catalog information showing dimensions, colors, and\n          configurations.\n\n   C.     Samples: Submit two samples of each wiring device and wall plate illustrating materials, construction,\n          color, and finish.\n\n1.04      QUALIFICATIONS\n\n   A.     Manufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this section with minimum\n          three years documented experience.\n\n1.05      EXTRA MATERIALS\n\n   A.     Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout Requirements:\n          Spare parts and maintenance products.\n\n   B.     Furnish two (2) of each style, size, and finish wall plate.\n\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n\n2.01      UNIFORMITY OF MANUFACTURER\n\n   A.     Products provided under this Section shall be from one manufacturer for identical catalog items (i.e.,\n          receptacles); wherever possible, provide uniformity of manufacturer for similar types of items.\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                                                26 27 26 - 1\nProject No. 26-2112-000                               Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n   B.     Plugs shall be of same manufacturer and grade as receptacles.\n\n   C.     Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of the following:\n          1.    Cooper Wiring Devices (abbreviated Cooper)\n          2.    Hubbell\n          3.    Pass & Seymour (abbreviated P & S)\n          4.    Leviton\n          5.    Curbell\n\n2.02      WALL SWITCHES\n\n   A.     General Requirements:\n          1.     Heavy-duty, AC only general-use snap switch, quiet operation type.\n          2.     Voltage: 120/277 volts, AC.\n          3.     Current: 20 amperes.\n          4.     Horsepower rating: 1 HP@120V; 2 HP@277V.\n          5.     Body and Handle: Decora style, thermoplastic with a nylon toggle handle. Handle color shall be\n                 selected by the Architect from the manufacturer’s standard colors.\n          6.     Switch shall be mounted on a plated steel yoke with a grounding screw.\n\n   B.     Switch Types: Switch types and manufacturer's catalog numbers as follows:\n\n                                               Manufacturer's Catalog Numbers\n                      Description                 Hubbell             P&S / Legrand\n                      Single Pole                   2121                 2621\n                      Double Pole                   2122                 2622\n                      Three-Way                     2123                 2623\n                      Four-Way                      2124                 2624\n\n   C.     Patient Room Low Voltage Lighting Control.\n          1.      Low Voltage Controller Wall Switch: Curbell WPA-1000-001\n          2.      Low Voltage Controller: Curbell LVC-2000-004\n\n2.03      RECEPTACLES\n\n   A.     General Requirements:\n          1.     Wide double blade contacts designed to maintain positive pressure against both sides of plug or\n                 cap having flat fingers. Contacts shall be solid brass.\n          2.     Polarized grounding type with grounding contacts bonded to receptacle mounting strap or\n                 housing, except isolated ground receptacles. Mounting strap shall be plated steel.\n          3.     Contacts separated by impact resisting molded plastic insulating material.\n          4.     Receptacles shall be back and side wired, provide a green base ground screw terminal and a\n                 nylon face.\n          5.     Locking devices, where specified, to \"lock\" cap in place with simple twisting motion.\n          6.     Receptacles shall be Decora style. Normal power receptacles shall be gray. Receptacles\n                 connected to emergency panelboards shall be red, illuminated face.\n          7.     Hospital grade type receptacles shall be used in all areas of the facility (non-patient and patient\n                 areas).\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                                                26 27 26 - 2\nProject No. 26-2112-000                               Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n          8.      Emergency receptacles shall be located in main service electrical rooms, substation rooms, ATS\n                  rooms, emergency paralleling switchgear rooms, and fuel oil pump rooms.\n          9.      Duplex emergency receptacles shall be located next to each sump and ejector pit.\n          10.     All receptacles that are accessible to the general public shall be tamper-proof.\n          11.     Receptacles must be GFCI type within 6 feet of sinks.\n\n   B.     Hospital Grade Receptacle Types: Rating in amperes, number of poles and wires, voltage, NEMA\n          configuration, description and manufacturer's catalog numbers as follows:\n                                                                             Manufacturer's Catalog Numbers\n          Rating                        NEMA             Description               Hubbell          P&S / Legrand\n           20A, 2P, 3W, 125V              5-20R        Duplex Illuminated            HBL8300IL                8300IL\n                                                             Face\n\n           20A, 2P, 3W, 125V              5-20R       Duplex Ground Fault           GFRST83IL                2097HG\n                                                       Circuit Interrupter\n                                                       Illuminated Face\n\n           20A, 2P, 3W, 125VAC /          5-20R        Dual USB Type A              USB8300A5             TR8300HUSB\n           5VDC, 3.1A – 5A                            Charger with Tamper-\n                                                        Resistant Duplex\n                                                           Receptacle\n\n           125VAC, 5VDC, 4.2A –                        Four USB Charging                USB4             TM8USB4NICC\n           5A                                           Station – Type A                                      6\n\n2.04      WALL PLATES\n\n   A.     Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of the following:\n          1.    Hubbell, Inc.\n          2.    Pass & Seymour, Inc. / Legrand.\n\n   B.     Cover plate: Beveled metal, stainless steel 302/304 with metal mounting screws to matching the wiring\n          devices selected. Stainless steel finish plates shall be used in all patient areas. Color shall be as selected\n          by the Architect from the manufacturer’s standard colors. Number of gangs and configuration as\n          required to fit the devices used.\n\n   C.     Weatherproof Cover Plate: Gasketed thermoplastic with hinged gasketed device cover. Gaskets shall be\n          provided between the box and the cover mounting surface and between the mounting surface and the\n          hinged cover. Cover shall be capable of being closed with a plug inserted in the receptacle, and shall be\n          UL listed as \"Suitable for Wet Locations While in Use.\" Covers shall be TayMac or approved equal.\n\n2.05      MULTIOUTLET ASSEMBLY\n\n   A.     Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of the following:\n          1.    Pass & Seymour, Inc. / Legrand\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                                                26 27 26 - 3\nProject No. 26-2112-000                               Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n   B.     Multi-outlet Assembly: Sheet metal channel with fitted cover, with pre-wired receptacles, suitable for\n          use as multi-outlet assembly.\n\n   C.     Size: As indicated on Drawings.\n\n   D.     Receptacles: NEMA WD 6, type 5-20R, single receptacle.\n\n   E.     Receptacle Spacing: As indicated on Drawings.\n\n   F.     Receptacle Color: Gray.\n\n   G.     Channel Finish: Ivory.\n\n   H.     Fittings: Furnish manufacturer’s standard couplings, elbows, outlet and device boxes, and connectors.\n\n   I.     Information Technology multioutlet assemblies shall comply with NYU Langone Health IT Design\n          Standards.\n\n\nPART 3 - EXECUTION\n\n3.01      EXAMINATION\n\n   A.     Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Administrative Requirements:\n          Coordination and project conditions.\n\n   B.     Verify outlet boxes are installed at proper height.\n\n   C.     Verify wall openings are neatly cut and completely covered by wall plates.\n\n   D.     Verify branch circuit wiring installation is completed, tested, and ready for connection to wiring devices.\n\n3.02      PREPARATION"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":48,"aggregated":"SECTION 26 27 26\n\n                                                                                      WIRING DEVICES\n\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n\n1.01      SUMMARY\n\n   A.     Section includes:\n          1.     Wall switches\n          2.     Wall dimmers\n          3.     Receptacles\n          4.     Device plates and decorative box covers\n          5.     Multioutlet assembly\n\n   B.     Related Sections:\n          1.     Section 26 05 33 - Raceway and Boxes for Electrical Systems: Outlet boxes for wiring devices.\n\n1.02      REFERENCES\n          1.   NEMA WD 1 - General Requirements for Wiring Devices.\n          2.   NEMA WD 6 - Wiring Devices-Dimensional Requirements.\n\n1.03      SUBMITTALS\n\n   A.     Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures: Submittal\n          procedures.\n\n   B.     Product Data: Submit manufacturer's catalog information showing dimensions, colors, and\n          configurations.\n\n   C.     Samples: Submit two samples of each wiring device and wall plate illustrating materials, construction,\n          color, and finish.\n\n1.04      QUALIFICATIONS\n\n   A.     Manufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this section with minimum\n          three years documented experience.\n\n1.05      EXTRA MATERIALS\n\n   A.     Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout Requirements:\n          Spare parts and maintenance products.\n\n   B.     Furnish two (2) of each style, size, and finish wall plate.\n\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n\n2.01      UNIFORMITY OF MANUFACTURER\n\n   A.     Products provided under this Section shall be from one manufacturer for identical catalog items (i.e.,\n          receptacles); wherever possible, provide uniformity of manufacturer for similar types of items.\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                                                26 27 26 - 1\nProject No. 26-2112-000                               Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n   B.     Plugs shall be of same manufacturer and grade as receptacles.\n\n   C.     Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of the following:\n          1.    Cooper Wiring Devices (abbreviated Cooper)\n          2.    Hubbell\n          3.    Pass & Seymour (abbreviated P & S)\n          4.    Leviton\n          5.    Curbell\n\n2.02      WALL SWITCHES\n\n   A.     General Requirements:\n          1.     Heavy-duty, AC only general-use snap switch, quiet operation type.\n          2.     Voltage: 120/277 volts, AC.\n          3.     Current: 20 amperes.\n          4.     Horsepower rating: 1 HP@120V; 2 HP@277V.\n          5.     Body and Handle: Decora style, thermoplastic with a nylon toggle handle. Handle color shall be\n                 selected by the Architect from the manufacturer’s standard colors.\n          6.     Switch shall be mounted on a plated steel yoke with a grounding screw.\n\n   B.     Switch Types: Switch types and manufacturer's catalog numbers as follows:\n\n                                               Manufacturer's Catalog Numbers\n                      Description                 Hubbell             P&S / Legrand\n                      Single Pole                   2121                 2621\n                      Double Pole                   2122                 2622\n                      Three-Way                     2123                 2623\n                      Four-Way                      2124                 2624\n\n   C.     Patient Room Low Voltage Lighting Control.\n          1.      Low Voltage Controller Wall Switch: Curbell WPA-1000-001\n          2.      Low Voltage Controller: Curbell LVC-2000-004\n\n2.03      RECEPTACLES\n\n   A.     General Requirements:\n          1.     Wide double blade contacts designed to maintain positive pressure against both sides of plug or\n                 cap having flat fingers. Contacts shall be solid brass.\n          2.     Polarized grounding type with grounding contacts bonded to receptacle mounting strap or\n                 housing, except isolated ground receptacles. Mounting strap shall be plated steel.\n          3.     Contacts separated by impact resisting molded plastic insulating material.\n          4.     Receptacles shall be back and side wired, provide a green base ground screw terminal and a\n                 nylon face.\n          5.     Locking devices, where specified, to \"lock\" cap in place with simple twisting motion.\n          6.     Receptacles shall be Decora style. Normal power receptacles shall be gray. Receptacles\n                 connected to emergency panelboards shall be red, illuminated face.\n          7.     Hospital grade type receptacles shall be used in all areas of the facility (non-patient and patient\n                 areas).\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                                                26 27 26 - 2\nProject No. 26-2112-000                               Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n          8.      Emergency receptacles shall be located in main service electrical rooms, substation rooms, ATS\n                  rooms, emergency paralleling switchgear rooms, and fuel oil pump rooms.\n          9.      Duplex emergency receptacles shall be located next to each sump and ejector pit.\n          10.     All receptacles that are accessible to the general public shall be tamper-proof.\n          11.     Receptacles must be GFCI type within 6 feet of sinks.\n\n   B.     Hospital Grade Receptacle Types: Rating in amperes, number of poles and wires, voltage, NEMA\n          configuration, description and manufacturer's catalog numbers as follows:\n                                                                             Manufacturer's Catalog Numbers\n          Rating                        NEMA             Description               Hubbell          P&S / Legrand\n           20A, 2P, 3W, 125V              5-20R        Duplex Illuminated            HBL8300IL                8300IL\n                                                             Face\n\n           20A, 2P, 3W, 125V              5-20R       Duplex Ground Fault           GFRST83IL                2097HG\n                                                       Circuit Interrupter\n                                                       Illuminated Face\n\n           20A, 2P, 3W, 125VAC /          5-20R        Dual USB Type A              USB8300A5             TR8300HUSB\n           5VDC, 3.1A – 5A                            Charger with Tamper-\n                                                        Resistant Duplex\n                                                           Receptacle\n\n           125VAC, 5VDC, 4.2A –                        Four USB Charging                USB4             TM8USB4NICC\n           5A                                           Station – Type A                                      6\n\n2.04      WALL PLATES\n\n   A.     Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of the following:\n          1.    Hubbell, Inc.\n          2.    Pass & Seymour, Inc. / Legrand.\n\n   B.     Cover plate: Beveled metal, stainless steel 302/304 with metal mounting screws to matching the wiring\n          devices selected. Stainless steel finish plates shall be used in all patient areas. Color shall be as selected\n          by the Architect from the manufacturer’s standard colors. Number of gangs and configuration as\n          required to fit the devices used.\n\n   C.     Weatherproof Cover Plate: Gasketed thermoplastic with hinged gasketed device cover. Gaskets shall be\n          provided between the box and the cover mounting surface and between the mounting surface and the\n          hinged cover. Cover shall be capable of being closed with a plug inserted in the receptacle, and shall be\n          UL listed as \"Suitable for Wet Locations While in Use.\" Covers shall be TayMac or approved equal.\n\n2.05      MULTIOUTLET ASSEMBLY\n\n   A.     Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of the following:\n          1.    Pass & Seymour, Inc. / Legrand\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                                                26 27 26 - 3\nProject No. 26-2112-000                               Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n   B.     Multi-outlet Assembly: Sheet metal channel with fitted cover, with pre-wired receptacles, suitable for\n          use as multi-outlet assembly.\n\n   C.     Size: As indicated on Drawings.\n\n   D.     Receptacles: NEMA WD 6, type 5-20R, single receptacle.\n\n   E.     Receptacle Spacing: As indicated on Drawings.\n\n   F.     Receptacle Color: Gray.\n\n   G.     Channel Finish: Ivory.\n\n   H.     Fittings: Furnish manufacturer’s standard couplings, elbows, outlet and device boxes, and connectors.\n\n   I.     Information Technology multioutlet assemblies shall comply with NYU Langone Health IT Design\n          Standards.\n\n\nPART 3 - EXECUTION\n\n3.01      EXAMINATION\n\n   A.     Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Administrative Requirements:\n          Coordination and project conditions.\n\n   B.     Verify outlet boxes are installed at proper height.\n\n   C.     Verify wall openings are neatly cut and completely covered by wall plates.\n\n   D.     Verify branch circuit wiring installation is completed, tested, and ready for connection to wiring devices.\n\n3.02      PREPARATION","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138573971}}
{"type":"message","id":"964e89b0","parentId":"46caaea6","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:09:34.009Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_015J3P3iZsUShTCPGuFrBTGE","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SECTION 21 05 04\n\n                                           VALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\n\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n\n1.01    SUMMARY\n\n  A.    Section Includes: General Duty Valves for the following systems:\n        1.    Fire Suppression standpipes, sprinklers and equipment.\n\n  B.    Related Sections:\n        1.    Division 08 - Access Doors and Frames: Product requirements for access doors\n              for placement by this section.\n        2.    Division 09 - Painting and Coating: Product and execution requirements for\n              painting specified by this section.\n        3.    Section 21 05 03 - Pipes Tubes for Fire-Suppression Piping and Equipment:\n              Product requirements for piping for placement by this section.\n        4.    Section 21 05 05 - Hangers and Supports for Fire-Suppression Piping and\n              Equipment: Product requirements for pipe hangers and supports and firestopping\n              for placement by this section.\n        5.    Section 21 05 48 - Noise and Vibration Controls for Fire Suppression Piping and\n              Equipment: Product requirements for vibration isolation for placement by this\n              section.\n        6.    Section 21 12 00 - Fire Suppression Standpipes: Product requirements for fire\n              standpipe piping for placement by this section.\n        7.    Section 21 13 13 - Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems: Product requirements for wet\n              sprinkler piping for placement by this section.\n\n1.02    REFERENCES\n\n  A.    American Society of Mechanical Engineers.\n\n  B.    ASTM International.\n\n  C.    American Water Works Association:\n        1.   ASTM A 307 - Standard Specification for Carbon Steel Bolts and Studs, 60,000\n             psi Tensile.\n        2.   ASTM B 62 - Standard Specification for Composition Bronze or Ounce Metal\n             Casting.\n        3.   ASTM D 429 - Standard Test Methods for Rubber Property-Adhesion to Rigid\n             Substrates.\n        4.   ASTM B 763 - Standard Specification for Copper Alloy Sand Casting for Valve\n             Application.\n        5.   AWWA C 500 - Standard for Metal-Seated Gate Valves for Water Supply Service.\n        6.   AWWA C 509 - Standard for Resilient-Seated Gate Valves for Water Supply\n             Service.\n        7.   AWWA C 515- Standard for Reduced Wall, Resilient- Seated Gate Valves for\n             Water Supply Service.\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           VALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                               21 05 04 - 1\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n        8.    H. AWWA C 550 - Standard for Protective Epoxy Interior Coatings for Valves\n              and Hydrants.\n\n1.03    SUBMITTALS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures:\n        Submittal procedures.\n\n  B.    Shop Drawings: Indicate layout of piping systems, including equipment, critical\n        dimensions, and sizes.\n\n  C.    Product Data: Submit data on pipe materials and fittings. Submit manufacturers catalog\n        information.\n\n  D.    Design Data: Indicate pipe sizes. Indicate pipe sizing methods. Indicate calculations\n        used.\n\n  E.    Welders’ Certificate: Include welders’ certification of compliance with ASME Section IX.\n\n1.04    QUALITY ASSURANCE\n\n  A.    Perform Work in accordance with ASME B31.9 code for installation of piping systems\n        and ASME Section IX for welding materials and procedures.\n\n  B.    Perform Work in accordance with NYCBC.\n\n1.05    QUALIFICATIONS\n\n  A.    Manufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing Products specified in this\n        section with minimum three (3) years documented experience.\n\n  B.    Installer: Company specializing in performing work of this section with minimum five\n        (5) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\n  C.    Design pipe hangers and supports under direct supervision of Professional Engineer\n        experienced in design of this Work and licensed in the State of New York.\n\n1.06    DELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\n        Requirements for transporting, handling, storing, and protecting products.\n\n  B.    Furnish temporary end caps and closures on piping and fittings. Maintain in place until\n        installation.\n\n  C.    Protect piping from entry of foreign materials by temporary covers, completing sections\n        of the Work, and isolating parts of completed system.\n\n1.07    ENVIRONMENTAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\n        Environmental conditions affecting products on site.\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           VALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                               21 05 04 - 2\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n1.08    FIELD MEASUREMENTS\n\n  A.    Verify field measurements prior to fabrication.\n\n1.09    COORDINATION\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Administrative\n        Requirements: Requirements for coordination.\n\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n\n2.01    GENERAL\n\n  A.    All fire protection water control valves within the building shall be either wedge gate\n        valves with painted iron wheel handles, shall have gland followers in stuffing boxes,\n        and shall be constructed so that they may be repacked while open and under pressure;\n        or slow-closing quarter-turn gear-operated butterfly valves.\n\n  B.    All valves shall have the name of the manufacturer and working pressure cast or\n        stamped on body.\n\n  C.    All valves: to be U.L. listed and FM approved.\n\n  D.    All valves shall be with threaded or flanged ends as required by the piping system in\n        which they are installed.\n\n  E.    Valves shall be selected for a minimum working pressure or 200 psig.\n\n2.02    VALVES\n\n   A.   Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\n        the following:\n        1.     Milwaukee Valve Co.\n        2.     Crane Valve Co.\n        3.     Anvil International\n        4.     Nibco Inc.\n        5.     Mueller Co.\n        6.     Victaulic Co.\n\n  B.    Gate Valves:\n        1.    Up to and including 2 inches: Bronze body and trim, rising stem, hand wheel,\n              solid wedge or disc, threaded ends.\n        2.    Over 2 inches: Iron body, bronze trim, rising stem pre-grooved for mounting\n              tamper switch, hand wheel, OS&Y, solid rubber covered bronze or cast iron\n              wedge, flanged ends.\n        3.    Post Indicator Type: Iron body, bronze trim, non-rising stem with bolted bonnet,\n              solid bronze wedge, flanged ends, iron body indicator post assembly.\n        4.    Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by\n              one of the following:\n              a.     Crane\n              b.     Grinnell\n              c.     Jenkins\n              d.     Kennedy\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           VALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                               21 05 04 - 3\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n              e.     NIBCO\n              f.     Walworth\n\n\n\n  C.    Globe or Angle Valves:\n        1.    Up to and including 2 inches: Bronze body, bronze trim, rising stem and\n              handwheel, inside screw, renewable rubber disc, threaded ends, with back seating\n              capacity packable under pressure.\n        2.    Over 2 inches: Iron body, bronze trim, rising stem, handwheel, OS&Y, plug-type\n              disc, flanged ends, renewable seat and disc.\n\n  D.    Ball Valves:\n        1.    Up to and including 2 inches: Bronze two piece body, brass, chrome plated\n              bronze, or stainless steel ball, teflon seats and stuffing box ring, lever handle,\n              threaded ends with union.\n        2.    Over 2 inches: Manufacturers: Cast steel body, chrome plated steel ball, teflon\n              seat and stuffing box seals, lever handle, flanged.\n\n  E.    Butterfly Valves:\n        1.    Up to and including 2 inches: Bronze Body, Stainless steel disc, resilient\n              replaceable seat, grooved ends, extended neck, hand wheel and gear drive and\n              integral indicating device, and built-in tamper proof switch rated 10 amp at 115"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":37,"aggregated":"SECTION 21 05 04\n\n                                           VALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\n\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n\n1.01    SUMMARY\n\n  A.    Section Includes: General Duty Valves for the following systems:\n        1.    Fire Suppression standpipes, sprinklers and equipment.\n\n  B.    Related Sections:\n        1.    Division 08 - Access Doors and Frames: Product requirements for access doors\n              for placement by this section.\n        2.    Division 09 - Painting and Coating: Product and execution requirements for\n              painting specified by this section.\n        3.    Section 21 05 03 - Pipes Tubes for Fire-Suppression Piping and Equipment:\n              Product requirements for piping for placement by this section.\n        4.    Section 21 05 05 - Hangers and Supports for Fire-Suppression Piping and\n              Equipment: Product requirements for pipe hangers and supports and firestopping\n              for placement by this section.\n        5.    Section 21 05 48 - Noise and Vibration Controls for Fire Suppression Piping and\n              Equipment: Product requirements for vibration isolation for placement by this\n              section.\n        6.    Section 21 12 00 - Fire Suppression Standpipes: Product requirements for fire\n              standpipe piping for placement by this section.\n        7.    Section 21 13 13 - Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems: Product requirements for wet\n              sprinkler piping for placement by this section.\n\n1.02    REFERENCES\n\n  A.    American Society of Mechanical Engineers.\n\n  B.    ASTM International.\n\n  C.    American Water Works Association:\n        1.   ASTM A 307 - Standard Specification for Carbon Steel Bolts and Studs, 60,000\n             psi Tensile.\n        2.   ASTM B 62 - Standard Specification for Composition Bronze or Ounce Metal\n             Casting.\n        3.   ASTM D 429 - Standard Test Methods for Rubber Property-Adhesion to Rigid\n             Substrates.\n        4.   ASTM B 763 - Standard Specification for Copper Alloy Sand Casting for Valve\n             Application.\n        5.   AWWA C 500 - Standard for Metal-Seated Gate Valves for Water Supply Service.\n        6.   AWWA C 509 - Standard for Resilient-Seated Gate Valves for Water Supply\n             Service.\n        7.   AWWA C 515- Standard for Reduced Wall, Resilient- Seated Gate Valves for\n             Water Supply Service.\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           VALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                               21 05 04 - 1\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n        8.    H. AWWA C 550 - Standard for Protective Epoxy Interior Coatings for Valves\n              and Hydrants.\n\n1.03    SUBMITTALS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures:\n        Submittal procedures.\n\n  B.    Shop Drawings: Indicate layout of piping systems, including equipment, critical\n        dimensions, and sizes.\n\n  C.    Product Data: Submit data on pipe materials and fittings. Submit manufacturers catalog\n        information.\n\n  D.    Design Data: Indicate pipe sizes. Indicate pipe sizing methods. Indicate calculations\n        used.\n\n  E.    Welders’ Certificate: Include welders’ certification of compliance with ASME Section IX.\n\n1.04    QUALITY ASSURANCE\n\n  A.    Perform Work in accordance with ASME B31.9 code for installation of piping systems\n        and ASME Section IX for welding materials and procedures.\n\n  B.    Perform Work in accordance with NYCBC.\n\n1.05    QUALIFICATIONS\n\n  A.    Manufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing Products specified in this\n        section with minimum three (3) years documented experience.\n\n  B.    Installer: Company specializing in performing work of this section with minimum five\n        (5) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\n  C.    Design pipe hangers and supports under direct supervision of Professional Engineer\n        experienced in design of this Work and licensed in the State of New York.\n\n1.06    DELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\n        Requirements for transporting, handling, storing, and protecting products.\n\n  B.    Furnish temporary end caps and closures on piping and fittings. Maintain in place until\n        installation.\n\n  C.    Protect piping from entry of foreign materials by temporary covers, completing sections\n        of the Work, and isolating parts of completed system.\n\n1.07    ENVIRONMENTAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\n        Environmental conditions affecting products on site.\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           VALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                               21 05 04 - 2\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n1.08    FIELD MEASUREMENTS\n\n  A.    Verify field measurements prior to fabrication.\n\n1.09    COORDINATION\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Administrative\n        Requirements: Requirements for coordination.\n\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n\n2.01    GENERAL\n\n  A.    All fire protection water control valves within the building shall be either wedge gate\n        valves with painted iron wheel handles, shall have gland followers in stuffing boxes,\n        and shall be constructed so that they may be repacked while open and under pressure;\n        or slow-closing quarter-turn gear-operated butterfly valves.\n\n  B.    All valves shall have the name of the manufacturer and working pressure cast or\n        stamped on body.\n\n  C.    All valves: to be U.L. listed and FM approved.\n\n  D.    All valves shall be with threaded or flanged ends as required by the piping system in\n        which they are installed.\n\n  E.    Valves shall be selected for a minimum working pressure or 200 psig.\n\n2.02    VALVES\n\n   A.   Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\n        the following:\n        1.     Milwaukee Valve Co.\n        2.     Crane Valve Co.\n        3.     Anvil International\n        4.     Nibco Inc.\n        5.     Mueller Co.\n        6.     Victaulic Co.\n\n  B.    Gate Valves:\n        1.    Up to and including 2 inches: Bronze body and trim, rising stem, hand wheel,\n              solid wedge or disc, threaded ends.\n        2.    Over 2 inches: Iron body, bronze trim, rising stem pre-grooved for mounting\n              tamper switch, hand wheel, OS&Y, solid rubber covered bronze or cast iron\n              wedge, flanged ends.\n        3.    Post Indicator Type: Iron body, bronze trim, non-rising stem with bolted bonnet,\n              solid bronze wedge, flanged ends, iron body indicator post assembly.\n        4.    Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by\n              one of the following:\n              a.     Crane\n              b.     Grinnell\n              c.     Jenkins\n              d.     Kennedy\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           VALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016                                               21 05 04 - 3\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n              e.     NIBCO\n              f.     Walworth\n\n\n\n  C.    Globe or Angle Valves:\n        1.    Up to and including 2 inches: Bronze body, bronze trim, rising stem and\n              handwheel, inside screw, renewable rubber disc, threaded ends, with back seating\n              capacity packable under pressure.\n        2.    Over 2 inches: Iron body, bronze trim, rising stem, handwheel, OS&Y, plug-type\n              disc, flanged ends, renewable seat and disc.\n\n  D.    Ball Valves:\n        1.    Up to and including 2 inches: Bronze two piece body, brass, chrome plated\n              bronze, or stainless steel ball, teflon seats and stuffing box ring, lever handle,\n              threaded ends with union.\n        2.    Over 2 inches: Manufacturers: Cast steel body, chrome plated steel ball, teflon\n              seat and stuffing box seals, lever handle, flanged.\n\n  E.    Butterfly Valves:\n        1.    Up to and including 2 inches: Bronze Body, Stainless steel disc, resilient\n              replaceable seat, grooved ends, extended neck, hand wheel and gear drive and\n              integral indicating device, and built-in tamper proof switch rated 10 amp at 115","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138574008}}
