{"type":"message","id":"cc48ed39","parentId":"4c15b2de","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:10:04.184Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_0176GbuWQxZGRHUNnMRwPJN3","toolName":"process","content":[{"type":"text","text":"         FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n=== 11202205_Specifications_V3_Part1 (1).pdf ===\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\n21 30 00         Fire Pumps\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                                                                  Selective Demolition\n=== 11202205_Specifications_V3_Part2.pdf ===\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\n=== 11202205_Specifications_V3_Part3.pdf ===\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\n  A.    Vertical Distance From Fire Pump:\n=== Abatement Specifications_Bellevue Fire Pump.pdf ===\n                                                                      FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                       ASBESTOS ABATEMENT\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                       ASBESTOS ABATEMENT\n              2.      Asbestos Survey Report performed by ATC Group Services titled Fire Pump &\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                       ASBESTOS ABATEMENT\n=== IFB - HHC PART 1 (4).pdf ===\n=== Section A-B_Revised.pdf ===\n                    1120220: Fire Pump & Standpipe\nPROJECT NAME:               11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump & Standpipe Replacement\n                             11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump &\nNAME OF PROJECT:        Fire Pump & Standpipe Replacement\n\n\nProcess exited with code 0."}],"details":{"status":"completed","sessionId":"gentle-trail","exitCode":0,"aggregated":"=== 11202205_Drawings_V2_Part1.pdf ===\n                                                                                           FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL PROJECT                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   BUILDING \"H\"\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            PATH                                                                                                        FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                          FIRE PUMP RM\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       CN11A                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          3. BUILD NEW FIRE PUMP ROOM ON MEZZANINE LEVEL INCLUDING, MECHANICAL\n=== 11202205_Drawings_V2_Part2.pdf ===\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Base Scope: Any scope required in the Cellar, Mezzanine Fire Pump Room, Janitor's                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             -         04/12/2024                  100% CONSTRUCTION DOCUMENTS\n       COPY ROOM                                                                                    OFFICE                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n          1        3RD FLOOR STAIR - NORTH                                                                                                                                       2          3RD FLOOR STAIR - WEST                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Base Scope: Any scope required in the Cellar, Mezzanine Fire Pump Room, Janitor's\n                                                             4W18                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n=== 11202205_Drawings_V2_Part3.pdf ===\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                         FIRE PUMP RM\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            FIRE PUMP RM\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n=== 11202205_Drawings_V2_Part4.pdf ===\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                             (2,155LBS FIRE PUMP)\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                              CAPPED PIPE                                                                CWR     CONDENSER WATER RETURN                                                      SECTION BC-1705.17, MC-606 AND MC-607.                            EXISTING DUCTS AND ASSOCIATED INSULATION. ALL NEW DUCTWORK                    FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                          STAIR N                                                                                       INFILTRATING INTO ADJACENT TENANT OR MECHANICAL AREAS. WELDING OR BURNING MUST BE                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n=== 11202205_Drawings_V2_Part5.pdf ===\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      CONTROLLED PANEL IN FIRE PUMP ROOM ON MEZZANINE\n                                                                                                                                                                                             7-EL-Q-5                                                                                                            REFER TO DRAWING E001.                                                     FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                  LAB                                                           8-EL-S-1                                                                                                 REFER TO DRAWING E001.                                                         FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n=== 11202205_Drawings_V2_Part6.pdf ===\n                                                                                                                                                                                     BED STOR.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                               SHAFT                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                        14-ST-N                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 2.                                   ALTERNATE 3: ANY SCOPE REQUIRED OR ASSOCIATED WITH THE                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  9                                               10                                                                                                                                            STAIR OF THE BUILDING SHALL BE PRICED SEPARATELY.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n=== 11202205_Drawings_V2_Part7.pdf ===\n                                                                                                            STAIR W                                                                          SHAFT                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 ALTERNATES:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                        17N29                            17N36                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ALTERNATES:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                   18N15                                                                                                                                18-SH-54                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 ELEV                                                                                                                                                                                                ALTERNATES:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n          20N31               OFFICE            OFFICE           20N24-59                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n=== 11202205_Drawings_V2_Part8.pdf ===\n                       17N29                             17N36                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            REFER TO STRUCTURAL DRAWINGS FOR MORE INFORMATION.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                       18N15                                                                                                                                         18-SH-54                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                           CORRIDOR                                                                                                                                      19-SH-30                                           SHAFT                                                                                                                                                                                                                   FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                20N31                OFFICE        OFFICE         20N24-59                                                                OFFICE                                                  20-SH-46          20-EL-K1                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                SHAFT                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\n=== 11202205_Specifications_V3_Part1 (1).pdf ===\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\n21 30 00         Fire Pumps\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                                                                  Selective Demolition\n=== 11202205_Specifications_V3_Part2.pdf ===\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project Alternate 1                                  WIRING DEVICES\n=== 11202205_Specifications_V3_Part3.pdf ===\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\n  A.    Vertical Distance From Fire Pump:\n=== Abatement Specifications_Bellevue Fire Pump.pdf ===\n                                                                      FIRE PUMP AND STANDPIPE REMOVAL\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                       ASBESTOS ABATEMENT\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                       ASBESTOS ABATEMENT\n              2.      Asbestos Survey Report performed by ATC Group Services titled Fire Pump &\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project                       ASBESTOS ABATEMENT\n=== IFB - HHC PART 1 (4).pdf ===\n=== Section A-B_Revised.pdf ===\n                    1120220: Fire Pump & Standpipe\nPROJECT NAME:               11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump & Standpipe Replacement\n                             11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump &\nNAME OF PROJECT:        Fire Pump & Standpipe Replacement\n","name":"cd /home/ec2-user/clawd/p...e/Bellevue - Standpipe"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138604180}}
{"type":"message","id":"17e05551","parentId":"cc48ed39","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:10:04.603Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01Q3P5JcCSDZ7eng11nyJt2m","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1:                                                                   SECTION 21 05 04\n619:                                                         END OF SECTION 21 05 04\n629:                                                                     SECTION 21 05 05\n1228:                                                        END OF SECTION 21 05 05\n1238:                                                                      SECTION 21 12 00\n1679:                                                        END OF SECTION 21 12 00"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":421,"aggregated":"1:                                                                   SECTION 21 05 04\n619:                                                         END OF SECTION 21 05 04\n629:                                                                     SECTION 21 05 05\n1228:                                                        END OF SECTION 21 05 05\n1238:                                                                      SECTION 21 12 00\n1679:                                                        END OF SECTION 21 12 00","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138604601}}
{"type":"message","id":"71009b23","parentId":"17e05551","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:10:10.914Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see that Section 21 30 00 Fire Pumps is listed in the Table of Contents (Part 1), but the spec content seems to be in Part 3 which only has up to Section 21 12 00. Let me check if the fire pump section is somewhere else or if I need to look in the drawings. Let me also extract more from the Standpipe section and then look at the drawings for FP sheets.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01FiMqnLeVEjoAtRVPnHAJPZ","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd \"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/Bellevue - Standpipe\" && pdftotext -layout \"11202205_Specifications_V3_Part3.pdf\" - 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1238,1679p'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_011qhYBjFFiAay2Jwq7iWmpP","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd \"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/Bellevue - Standpipe\" && pdfinfo 11202205_Drawings_V2_Part*.pdf 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"File:|Pages:\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":8,"output":334,"cacheRead":34189,"cacheWrite":944,"totalTokens":35475,"cost":{"input":0.00004,"output":0.00835,"cacheRead":0.0170945,"cacheWrite":0.0059,"total":0.0313845}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770138604603}}
{"type":"message","id":"073256cf","parentId":"71009b23","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:10:11.237Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01FiMqnLeVEjoAtRVPnHAJPZ","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SECTION 21 12 00\n\n                                            FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\n\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n\n1.01    SUMMARY\n\n  A.    Section includes entire standpipe system from fire department connection to fire hose\n        connection and the following:\n        1.    Complete wet fire standpipe system.\n        2.    Roof manifold.\n        3.    Angle Hose Valves.\n        4.    Fire Hose and Nozzles\n        5.    Accessories for Valves and Hoses.\n        6.    Hose Valve Cabinets\n        7.    Detention Locked Hose Valve Cabinets\n        8.    Painting and Identification of piping.\n        9.    Valve Supervisory Switches\n\n  B.    Related Sections:\n        1.    Division 08 - Access Doors and Frames: Product requirements for access doors\n              for placement by this section.\n        2.    Division 09 - Painting and Coating: Product and execution requirements for\n              painting specified by this section.\n        3.    Section 21 05 00 - Common Work Results for Fire Suppression: Product and\n              execution requirements for pipe, fittings, valves, hangers, supports, identification\n              and painting for placement by this section.\n        4.    Section 21 05 03 - Pipes Tubes for Fire-Suppression Piping and Equipment:\n              Product requirements for piping for placement by this section.\n        5.    Section 21 05 05 - Hangers and Supports for Fire-Suppression Piping and\n              Equipment: Product requirements for pipe hangers and supports and firestopping\n              for placement by this section.\n        6.    Section 21 13 13 - Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems: Product requirements for wet\n              sprinkler piping for placement by this section.\n\n1.02    REFERENCES\n\n  A.    FM Global:\n        1.   FM - Approval Guide, A Guide to Equipment, Materials & Services Approved\n             By Factory Mutual Research For Property Conservation.\n\n  B.    National Fire Protection Association:\n        1.    NFPA 14 - Standard for the Installation of Standpipe, Private Hydrants and Hose\n              Systems.\n\n1.03    SUBMITTALS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures:\n        Submittal procedures.\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n  B.    Shop Drawings: Indicate supports, components, accessories and sizes.\n\n  C.    Product Data: Submit manufacturer's catalog sheet for equipment indicating rough-in\n        size, finish, and accessories.\n\n  D.    Field Test Reports: Indicate compliance with specified performance.\n\n  E.    Manufacturer's Installation Instructions: Submit with product data.\n\n   F.   Manufacturer's Certificate: Certify products meet or exceed specified requirements.\n\n1.04    CLOSEOUT SUBMITTALS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\n        Requirements: Closeout procedures.\n\n  B.    Operation and Maintenance Data: Submit servicing requirements and test schedule.\n\n1.05    QUALITY ASSURANCE\n\n  A.    Perform Work in accordance with NYCBC.\n\n  B.    Maintain one (1) copy of each document on site.\n\n1.06    QUALIFICATIONS\n\n  A.    Manufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this\n        section with minimum three (3) years documented experience.\n\n  B.    Installer: Company specializing in performing Work of this section with minimum three\n        (3) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\n1.07    DELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\n        Requirements for transporting, handling, storing, and protecting products.\n\n  B.    Deliver and store products in shipping packaging until installation.\n\n1.08    WARRANTY\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\n        Requirements: Product warranties and product bonds.\n\n  B.    Furnish five-year manufacturer warranty for standpipes and valves.\n\n1.09    EXTRA MATERIALS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\n        Requirements: Spare parts and maintenance products.\n\n  B.    Furnish two (2) hose nozzles and hoses.\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 2\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n\n2.01    GENERAL\n\n  A.    All threads are to conform to NYC Fire Department requirements.\n\n2.02    PIPE ESCUTCHEONS\n\n  A.    Pipe escutcheons shall have an inside diameter closely fitting pipe outside diameter or\n        outside of pipe insulation where pipe is insulated. Select outside diameter of\n        escutcheon to completely cover pipe penetration hole in floors, walls, or ceilings; and\n        pipe sleeve extension, if any. Escutcheons shall be cast or sheet brass, solid or split-\n        hinged, with brass set screw. Provide chrome finish for occupied areas exposed to\n        view.\n\n2.03    PIPE SLEEVES\n\n  A.    Provide pipe sleeves of one of the following. Pipe sleeve must be appropriate type and\n        thickness for the UL firestopping assembly selected:\n        1.    Sheet-Metal: Fabricate from galvanized sheet metal; round tube closed with\n              snaplock joint, welded spiral seams, or welded longitudinal joint. Fabricate from\n              the following gauges: 3\" and smaller, 20 gage minimum; 4\" to 6\", 16 gage; over\n              6\", 14 gage minimum.\n        2.    Steel-Pipe: Fabricate from Schedule 40 galvanized steel pipe; remove burrs.\n        3.    Iron-Pipe: Fabricate from cast-iron or ductile-iron pipe; remove burrs.\n        4.    Firestop penetration materials for sealing sleeves shall be listed by Underwriters\n              Laboratories and if not listed have MEA or OTCR approval. The materials shall\n              be as specified in Section 07 27 0. For pipes passing through fire-rated floor,\n              cast-in place firestop device with Underwriters Laboratories listing, and if not\n              listed have MEA or OTCR approval, is permitted as an acceptable sleeve\n              alternative to a metallic sleeve with firestopping material. The cast-in place\n              device is a one-step firestopping process that does not require additional firestop\n              penetration materials for sealing the sleeves. The device shall be installed where\n              required for sleeving purposes. The cast-in place firestop device shall not be used\n              for wall applications.\n\n   B.   Materials for sealing space between each pipe and sleeve through non-rated interior\n        walls shall consist of mineral wool and sealant.\n\n2.04    FIRE HOSE VALVES AND CABINETS\n\n   A.   Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\n        the following:\n        1.     Potter Roemer\n        2.     WSA Inc.\n        3.     Croker.\n\n   B.   Cabinet: Suitable for 2-1/2” fire department valve and 1-1/2” hose rack assembly,\n        recessed, stainless steel 304 door with 20 gauge steel frame, dual horizontal panel, red\n        powder coat finish, fire rated tub insulated with Firespan 90 tested by UL and rated to\n        ASTM E814. Similar to Croker 1410 Series Fire-Rated hose cabinet, rated to 2 hours.\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 3\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n  C.    Locked Detention Cabinets: Constructed for maximum security facilities with 12 gauge\n        cold rolled steel. Mitered and ground smooth corners. Cabinet shall be powder coated\n        with thermally-fused polyester red finish. Heavy-duty continuous hinge. Door shall be\n        flush solid metal with security-type lock. Recessed cabinet. Potter Roemer model#\n        DC1810-F.\n\n  D.    Hose Connection Valve: Angle type; brass finish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 1-\n        1/2 inch reducer, thread to match fire department hardware, with threaded cap and chain\n        of brass finish. Hose valve shall conform to FDNY standards. Valves shall be similar\n        to Potter Roemer Fig. 4065 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5015. Cap with chain shall be similar\n        to Potter Roemer 4625 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5713. Threads shall be to NYC Fire\n        department specifications.\n\n  E.    Hose Rack Assembly:\n        1.   Similar to Croker Model 3307 Style N.\n        2.   UL 47, semiautomatic hose stations. Include brass rack nipple, hose rack, and\n             the following:\n             a.     Valve: UL 668, brass or bronze, 300-psig minimum pressure rating, 90-\n                    degree-angle-pattern hose valve with female NPS inlet and outlet, brass\n                    finish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 1-1/2 inch reducer, thread to\n                    match fire department hardware. Valve Operation: Nonadjustable type,\n                    unless pressure-regulating type is indicated. Hose Valve and Trim Finish:\n                    Polished chrome-plated.\n             b.     Hose Rack: Steel; Semi-automatic swinging type with pins for folding\n                    hose and water stop. Finish: Red enamel.\n             c.     Hose: NFPA 1961 and UL 219, lined fire hose, 1-1/2 inch diameter, 125\n                    feet long, of polyurethane lined synthetic hose; mildew and rot-resistant.\n             d.     Nozzle: UL 401, brass, combination fog, straight stream, and adjustable\n                    shut-off. Finish: polished brass.\n             e.     Drain Valves: UL 1726.\n\n  F.    Pressure Restricting Hose Valve:\n        1.    Pressure-Restricting Hose Valve Class: NPS 2-1/2” and 1-1/2”, brass, adjustable\n              similar to Croker model 5560 set at 100 psi.\n\n2.05    FIRE DEPARTMENT LOBBY HOSE CABINET\n\n  A.    Fire Department Lobby Hose Cabinet:\n        1.    Cabinet, with built-in storage shelf for storing below listed equipment, shall be\n              recessed type, 20-gage steel body and baked white polyester finish inside.\n              Exposed trim and door shall be 18-gage, with continuous steel hinge (brass pin).\n              Cabinet door shall have duo-panel wire inserted clear glass. Door shall be hinged\n              right or left as required with lock and key in a key cabinet. Cabinet shall be\n              Potter Roemer 1302 or Croker Corp. Fig. 2190. The cabinet shall be labeled “For\n              Fire Department Use Only”. Final size dependent on amount of material to be\n              placed in cabinet.\n              a.     Class I standpipe requires the installation of a storage cabinet on the main\n                     entrance floor. Where one standpipe riser is installed in the building, the\n                     cabinet shall contain at least one fog nozzle, one 1½” spanner wrench, one\n                     2½” wrench, one 2½”x 1.5” non-swivel reducing coupling, and 125’ of\n                     1½” hose. Also provide one pressure restricting device to limit static and\n                     residual pressures at the outlet of the hose connection to 100 psi. For\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 4\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n                     buildings over 10 stories, provide another cabinet at the tenth floor (and\n                     every ten floors thereafter). Where two or more standpipe risers are\n                     installed in the building, at least two of the required items of equipment\n                     listed herein shall be provided.\n              b.     The equipment specified for the Lobby Storage Cabinet shall be of one\n                     manufacturer for each complete unit.\n\n  B.    Lobby Key Storage Cabinet:\n        1.   The key to the “Lobby Storage Cabinet” shall be kept in a locked “Key Storage\n             Cabinet”, openable only by a Fire Department city wide standard key. The\n             cabinet shall be labeled “For Fire Department Use Only”. A metal sign stating\n             where the storage cabinet is located shall be placed in each stair enclosure on the\n             main entrance and on each floor. The cabinet shall hold a key for the lobby\n             storage cabinet. Cabinet installation requires 5”x5”x3” wall opening. Cabinet\n             shall be Potter Roemer model #1950 NYFD Yale lock #SYA1, or Croker Fig.\n             2928 or Fig. 2920.\n\n2.06    FIRE DEPARTMENT CONNECTION\n\n  A.    Flush type shall be of the size indicated on drawings. Fire Department connections shall\n        be polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves and cast iron plugs painted\n        yellow with brass chain and with polished plate lettered “COMBINATION\n        STANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter inscription shall be either an\n        integral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate securely fastened to or above the\n        Fire Department connection. Flush type shall be Potter Roemer Fig. 5020G Series\n        (THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig. 6030 Series (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads\n        shall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\n  B.    Exposed type shall be of the size indicated on the drawings. Fire Department\n        connections shall be polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves, pin lug\n        swivels, plugs and chains painted yellow and with polished brass wall plate lettered\n        “COMBINATION STANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter\n        inscription shall be either an integral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate\n        securely fastened to or above the Fire Department connection. Expose type shall be\n        Potter- Roemer, Fig. 5750 Series (THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig 6430\n        Series (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads shall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\n  C.    Outlets: Two-way with fire department thread size. Threaded dust-cap and chain of\n        matching material and finish.\n\n  D.    Drain: 3/4 inch automatic drip pipe to outside or connected to drain via indirect drain.\n\n  E.    Where a fence encloses a portion of the building containing a Fire Department\n        connection, Contractor shall provide and secure to the fence directly opposite the Fire\n        Department connection a steel sign containing the following wording: \"F.D. Fire\n        Department Connection located...Feet behind Sign.\" Sign shall be finished in porcelain\n        enamel with 1-inch red letters on white background.\n\n2.07    ROOF MANIFOLD FIRE DEPARTMENT OUTLET CONNECTION:\n\n  A.    Style: Free standing, angle inlet. Cast brass body.\n\n  B.    Connections: 6-inch female NPT inlet and four (4) 2-1/2-inch male NPT outlets.\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 5\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n  C.    Roof outlet shall be fitted with three cast brass valves.\n\n2.08    PRESSURE GAUGES\n\n   A.   Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\n        the following:\n        1.     Terice Model 600C\n        2.     Weksler Model Regal\n        3.     AGF Manufacturing Co.\n        4.     AMETEK, Inc.; U.S. Gauge.\n        5.     Dresser Equipment Group; Instrument Div.\n\n   B.   Description: UL 393, 4-1/2-inch- diameter, dial pressure gage with range of -10 to 300\n        psig minimum. Cast brass, type ‘L’ case, glass covered, and phosphor bronze bourdon\n        type tube. Include caption \"WATER\" on dial face.\n\n2.09    AUTOMATIC BALL DRIP\n\n   A.   Automatic Ball Drip shall be 3/4\" Potter-Roemer Fig. 5982 or Croker Corp. Fig. 6781.\n\n2.10    LADDERS\n\n   A.   Provide permanent heavy steel ladders to provide access to valves in accordance with\n        the code requirements. Ladders shall be of width and height required, shall be made of\n        heavy steel bars and heavy rungs and shall be permanently fastened at location. Where\n        the shut-off valve adjacent to the sprinkler alarm valve is located higher than 6' above\n        the floor, ladder shall be provided where directed.\n\n2.11    PAINTING\n\n  A.    Paints used on dedicated piping to combination sprinkler and standpipe shall not:\n        1.     Exceed the VOC content limits established in the Green Seal Standard GS-11\n               Paints, first edition, May 20, 1993.\n        2.     Exceed the VOC content limit of 250 g/L established in the Green Seal Standard\n               GC-03, Anti-Corrosive paints, second edition, January 7, 1997.\n\n  B.    Provide colors indicated in Paragraph 3.04\n        1.    First (1st) coat – Alkyd Vinyl Acrylic – Latex Primer – 1.2 Mills DFT\n        2.    Second (2nd) coat – Semi-Gloss Vinyl Acrylic Latex – Enamel – 1.3 Mills DFT\n\n2.12    VALVE SUPERVISORY SWITCHES\n\n  A.    Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\n        the following:\n        1.     Potter Electric Signal Co. Model OSYSU-2\n        2.     Fire-Lite Alarms, Inc.; a Honeywell company.\n        3.     Kennedy Valve; a division of McWane, Inc.\n        4.     System Sensor; a Honeywell company.\n\n  B.    Standard: UL 346.\n\n  C.    Type: Electrically supervised.\n\n  D.    Components: Single-pole, double-throw switch with normally closed contacts.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 6\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n  E.    Design: Signals that controlled valve is in other than fully open position.\n\n  F.    Locate on each valve as designated on the drawings. Switches shall be mounted so not\n        to interfere with the normal operation of the valve and shall be adjusted to operate\n        within two revolutions of the valve control or when the stem has moved no more than\n        one-fifth of the distance from its normal position. The switch mechanism shall be\n        contained in a weatherproof die-cast aluminum housing which shall provide 3/4” tapped\n        conduit entrance and incorporate the necessary facilities for attachment to the valve.\n        Switch housings shall be finished in red baked enamel.\n\n\nPART 3 - EXECUTION\n\n3.01    EXAMINATION\n\n   A.   Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Administrative\n        Requirements: Coordination and project conditions.\n\n  B.    Verify blocking in place for cabinet installation.\n\n3.02    INSTALLATION\n\n  A.    Install in accordance with NFPA 14.\n\n  B.    Install cabinets plumb and level. Secure to adjacent surfaces. Establish top of cabinet\n        (inside horizontal) surface 66 inches above finished floor.\n\n   C.   Install hose station valve in cabinet at 60 inches above floor.\n\n   D.    Connect standpipe system to water source separate from domestic water connection.\n\n   E.    Where static pressure exceeds 100 psi at any hose station, furnish pressure orifice disc\n         in discharge of hose station valve to prevent pressure on hose exceeding 90 psi.\n\n   F.    Install three-way fire department outlet on roof.\n\n3.03     FIELD QUALITY CONTROL\n\n   A.   Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Quality Requirements,\n        and Execution and Closeout Requirements: Field inspecting, testing, adjusting and\n        balancing.\n\n   B.    Test entire system in accordance with NFPA 14.\n\n   C.    Require test be witnessed by Fire Marshall, Authority having jurisdiction and Owner's\n         insurance underwriter.\n\n3.04     TESTING\n\n   A.   Hydrostatic Testing: After flushing system, test standpipe piping hydrostatically, for\n        period of 2 hour, at not less than 300 psi or 50 psi in excess of the system working\n        pressure, whichever is greater. Check system for leakage of joints. The test pressure\n        shall be read from a gage located at the low point of each system or zone being tested.\n        1.     Repair or replace piping system as required to eliminate leakage.\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 7\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n        2.    Test the entire fire protection installation, including fire alarm system, in\n              accordance with the requirements of the NYC Fire Code and give at least 2 days\n              advance notice in writing of tests and inspections to the Construction Inspection\n              Division and the Authority. Tests shall be conducted in the presence of the any\n              public authority having jurisdiction. All tests shall be performed as part of this\n              contract.\n\n3.05    FIELD PAINTING\n\n  A.    Protect sprinkler heads during painting with small paper bags. Painting of sprinkler/ fire\n        standpipe piping, hangers, and all other items and accessories shall conform to the code\n        requirements.\n\n  B.    Paint standpipes in accordance with Specification Section 21 05 00.\n\n3.06    CLEANING\n\n   A.   Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\n        Requirements: Final cleaning.\n\n   B.   Flush entire system of foreign matter.\n\n\n                                                        END OF SECTION 21 12 00"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":318,"aggregated":"SECTION 21 12 00\n\n                                            FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\n\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n\n1.01    SUMMARY\n\n  A.    Section includes entire standpipe system from fire department connection to fire hose\n        connection and the following:\n        1.    Complete wet fire standpipe system.\n        2.    Roof manifold.\n        3.    Angle Hose Valves.\n        4.    Fire Hose and Nozzles\n        5.    Accessories for Valves and Hoses.\n        6.    Hose Valve Cabinets\n        7.    Detention Locked Hose Valve Cabinets\n        8.    Painting and Identification of piping.\n        9.    Valve Supervisory Switches\n\n  B.    Related Sections:\n        1.    Division 08 - Access Doors and Frames: Product requirements for access doors\n              for placement by this section.\n        2.    Division 09 - Painting and Coating: Product and execution requirements for\n              painting specified by this section.\n        3.    Section 21 05 00 - Common Work Results for Fire Suppression: Product and\n              execution requirements for pipe, fittings, valves, hangers, supports, identification\n              and painting for placement by this section.\n        4.    Section 21 05 03 - Pipes Tubes for Fire-Suppression Piping and Equipment:\n              Product requirements for piping for placement by this section.\n        5.    Section 21 05 05 - Hangers and Supports for Fire-Suppression Piping and\n              Equipment: Product requirements for pipe hangers and supports and firestopping\n              for placement by this section.\n        6.    Section 21 13 13 - Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems: Product requirements for wet\n              sprinkler piping for placement by this section.\n\n1.02    REFERENCES\n\n  A.    FM Global:\n        1.   FM - Approval Guide, A Guide to Equipment, Materials & Services Approved\n             By Factory Mutual Research For Property Conservation.\n\n  B.    National Fire Protection Association:\n        1.    NFPA 14 - Standard for the Installation of Standpipe, Private Hydrants and Hose\n              Systems.\n\n1.03    SUBMITTALS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures:\n        Submittal procedures.\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n  B.    Shop Drawings: Indicate supports, components, accessories and sizes.\n\n  C.    Product Data: Submit manufacturer's catalog sheet for equipment indicating rough-in\n        size, finish, and accessories.\n\n  D.    Field Test Reports: Indicate compliance with specified performance.\n\n  E.    Manufacturer's Installation Instructions: Submit with product data.\n\n   F.   Manufacturer's Certificate: Certify products meet or exceed specified requirements.\n\n1.04    CLOSEOUT SUBMITTALS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\n        Requirements: Closeout procedures.\n\n  B.    Operation and Maintenance Data: Submit servicing requirements and test schedule.\n\n1.05    QUALITY ASSURANCE\n\n  A.    Perform Work in accordance with NYCBC.\n\n  B.    Maintain one (1) copy of each document on site.\n\n1.06    QUALIFICATIONS\n\n  A.    Manufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this\n        section with minimum three (3) years documented experience.\n\n  B.    Installer: Company specializing in performing Work of this section with minimum three\n        (3) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\n1.07    DELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\n        Requirements for transporting, handling, storing, and protecting products.\n\n  B.    Deliver and store products in shipping packaging until installation.\n\n1.08    WARRANTY\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\n        Requirements: Product warranties and product bonds.\n\n  B.    Furnish five-year manufacturer warranty for standpipes and valves.\n\n1.09    EXTRA MATERIALS\n\n  A.    Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\n        Requirements: Spare parts and maintenance products.\n\n  B.    Furnish two (2) hose nozzles and hoses.\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 2\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n\n2.01    GENERAL\n\n  A.    All threads are to conform to NYC Fire Department requirements.\n\n2.02    PIPE ESCUTCHEONS\n\n  A.    Pipe escutcheons shall have an inside diameter closely fitting pipe outside diameter or\n        outside of pipe insulation where pipe is insulated. Select outside diameter of\n        escutcheon to completely cover pipe penetration hole in floors, walls, or ceilings; and\n        pipe sleeve extension, if any. Escutcheons shall be cast or sheet brass, solid or split-\n        hinged, with brass set screw. Provide chrome finish for occupied areas exposed to\n        view.\n\n2.03    PIPE SLEEVES\n\n  A.    Provide pipe sleeves of one of the following. Pipe sleeve must be appropriate type and\n        thickness for the UL firestopping assembly selected:\n        1.    Sheet-Metal: Fabricate from galvanized sheet metal; round tube closed with\n              snaplock joint, welded spiral seams, or welded longitudinal joint. Fabricate from\n              the following gauges: 3\" and smaller, 20 gage minimum; 4\" to 6\", 16 gage; over\n              6\", 14 gage minimum.\n        2.    Steel-Pipe: Fabricate from Schedule 40 galvanized steel pipe; remove burrs.\n        3.    Iron-Pipe: Fabricate from cast-iron or ductile-iron pipe; remove burrs.\n        4.    Firestop penetration materials for sealing sleeves shall be listed by Underwriters\n              Laboratories and if not listed have MEA or OTCR approval. The materials shall\n              be as specified in Section 07 27 0. For pipes passing through fire-rated floor,\n              cast-in place firestop device with Underwriters Laboratories listing, and if not\n              listed have MEA or OTCR approval, is permitted as an acceptable sleeve\n              alternative to a metallic sleeve with firestopping material. The cast-in place\n              device is a one-step firestopping process that does not require additional firestop\n              penetration materials for sealing the sleeves. The device shall be installed where\n              required for sleeving purposes. The cast-in place firestop device shall not be used\n              for wall applications.\n\n   B.   Materials for sealing space between each pipe and sleeve through non-rated interior\n        walls shall consist of mineral wool and sealant.\n\n2.04    FIRE HOSE VALVES AND CABINETS\n\n   A.   Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\n        the following:\n        1.     Potter Roemer\n        2.     WSA Inc.\n        3.     Croker.\n\n   B.   Cabinet: Suitable for 2-1/2” fire department valve and 1-1/2” hose rack assembly,\n        recessed, stainless steel 304 door with 20 gauge steel frame, dual horizontal panel, red\n        powder coat finish, fire rated tub insulated with Firespan 90 tested by UL and rated to\n        ASTM E814. Similar to Croker 1410 Series Fire-Rated hose cabinet, rated to 2 hours.\n\n\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 3\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n  C.    Locked Detention Cabinets: Constructed for maximum security facilities with 12 gauge\n        cold rolled steel. Mitered and ground smooth corners. Cabinet shall be powder coated\n        with thermally-fused polyester red finish. Heavy-duty continuous hinge. Door shall be\n        flush solid metal with security-type lock. Recessed cabinet. Potter Roemer model#\n        DC1810-F.\n\n  D.    Hose Connection Valve: Angle type; brass finish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 1-\n        1/2 inch reducer, thread to match fire department hardware, with threaded cap and chain\n        of brass finish. Hose valve shall conform to FDNY standards. Valves shall be similar\n        to Potter Roemer Fig. 4065 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5015. Cap with chain shall be similar\n        to Potter Roemer 4625 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5713. Threads shall be to NYC Fire\n        department specifications.\n\n  E.    Hose Rack Assembly:\n        1.   Similar to Croker Model 3307 Style N.\n        2.   UL 47, semiautomatic hose stations. Include brass rack nipple, hose rack, and\n             the following:\n             a.     Valve: UL 668, brass or bronze, 300-psig minimum pressure rating, 90-\n                    degree-angle-pattern hose valve with female NPS inlet and outlet, brass\n                    finish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 1-1/2 inch reducer, thread to\n                    match fire department hardware. Valve Operation: Nonadjustable type,\n                    unless pressure-regulating type is indicated. Hose Valve and Trim Finish:\n                    Polished chrome-plated.\n             b.     Hose Rack: Steel; Semi-automatic swinging type with pins for folding\n                    hose and water stop. Finish: Red enamel.\n             c.     Hose: NFPA 1961 and UL 219, lined fire hose, 1-1/2 inch diameter, 125\n                    feet long, of polyurethane lined synthetic hose; mildew and rot-resistant.\n             d.     Nozzle: UL 401, brass, combination fog, straight stream, and adjustable\n                    shut-off. Finish: polished brass.\n             e.     Drain Valves: UL 1726.\n\n  F.    Pressure Restricting Hose Valve:\n        1.    Pressure-Restricting Hose Valve Class: NPS 2-1/2” and 1-1/2”, brass, adjustable\n              similar to Croker model 5560 set at 100 psi.\n\n2.05    FIRE DEPARTMENT LOBBY HOSE CABINET\n\n  A.    Fire Department Lobby Hose Cabinet:\n        1.    Cabinet, with built-in storage shelf for storing below listed equipment, shall be\n              recessed type, 20-gage steel body and baked white polyester finish inside.\n              Exposed trim and door shall be 18-gage, with continuous steel hinge (brass pin).\n              Cabinet door shall have duo-panel wire inserted clear glass. Door shall be hinged\n              right or left as required with lock and key in a key cabinet. Cabinet shall be\n              Potter Roemer 1302 or Croker Corp. Fig. 2190. The cabinet shall be labeled “For\n              Fire Department Use Only”. Final size dependent on amount of material to be\n              placed in cabinet.\n              a.     Class I standpipe requires the installation of a storage cabinet on the main\n                     entrance floor. Where one standpipe riser is installed in the building, the\n                     cabinet shall contain at least one fog nozzle, one 1½” spanner wrench, one\n                     2½” wrench, one 2½”x 1.5” non-swivel reducing coupling, and 125’ of\n                     1½” hose. Also provide one pressure restricting device to limit static and\n                     residual pressures at the outlet of the hose connection to 100 psi. For\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 4\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n                     buildings over 10 stories, provide another cabinet at the tenth floor (and\n                     every ten floors thereafter). Where two or more standpipe risers are\n                     installed in the building, at least two of the required items of equipment\n                     listed herein shall be provided.\n              b.     The equipment specified for the Lobby Storage Cabinet shall be of one\n                     manufacturer for each complete unit.\n\n  B.    Lobby Key Storage Cabinet:\n        1.   The key to the “Lobby Storage Cabinet” shall be kept in a locked “Key Storage\n             Cabinet”, openable only by a Fire Department city wide standard key. The\n             cabinet shall be labeled “For Fire Department Use Only”. A metal sign stating\n             where the storage cabinet is located shall be placed in each stair enclosure on the\n             main entrance and on each floor. The cabinet shall hold a key for the lobby\n             storage cabinet. Cabinet installation requires 5”x5”x3” wall opening. Cabinet\n             shall be Potter Roemer model #1950 NYFD Yale lock #SYA1, or Croker Fig.\n             2928 or Fig. 2920.\n\n2.06    FIRE DEPARTMENT CONNECTION\n\n  A.    Flush type shall be of the size indicated on drawings. Fire Department connections shall\n        be polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves and cast iron plugs painted\n        yellow with brass chain and with polished plate lettered “COMBINATION\n        STANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter inscription shall be either an\n        integral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate securely fastened to or above the\n        Fire Department connection. Flush type shall be Potter Roemer Fig. 5020G Series\n        (THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig. 6030 Series (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads\n        shall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\n  B.    Exposed type shall be of the size indicated on the drawings. Fire Department\n        connections shall be polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves, pin lug\n        swivels, plugs and chains painted yellow and with polished brass wall plate lettered\n        “COMBINATION STANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter\n        inscription shall be either an integral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate\n        securely fastened to or above the Fire Department connection. Expose type shall be\n        Potter- Roemer, Fig. 5750 Series (THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig 6430\n        Series (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads shall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\n  C.    Outlets: Two-way with fire department thread size. Threaded dust-cap and chain of\n        matching material and finish.\n\n  D.    Drain: 3/4 inch automatic drip pipe to outside or connected to drain via indirect drain.\n\n  E.    Where a fence encloses a portion of the building containing a Fire Department\n        connection, Contractor shall provide and secure to the fence directly opposite the Fire\n        Department connection a steel sign containing the following wording: \"F.D. Fire\n        Department Connection located...Feet behind Sign.\" Sign shall be finished in porcelain\n        enamel with 1-inch red letters on white background.\n\n2.07    ROOF MANIFOLD FIRE DEPARTMENT OUTLET CONNECTION:\n\n  A.    Style: Free standing, angle inlet. Cast brass body.\n\n  B.    Connections: 6-inch female NPT inlet and four (4) 2-1/2-inch male NPT outlets.\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 5\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n  C.    Roof outlet shall be fitted with three cast brass valves.\n\n2.08    PRESSURE GAUGES\n\n   A.   Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\n        the following:\n        1.     Terice Model 600C\n        2.     Weksler Model Regal\n        3.     AGF Manufacturing Co.\n        4.     AMETEK, Inc.; U.S. Gauge.\n        5.     Dresser Equipment Group; Instrument Div.\n\n   B.   Description: UL 393, 4-1/2-inch- diameter, dial pressure gage with range of -10 to 300\n        psig minimum. Cast brass, type ‘L’ case, glass covered, and phosphor bronze bourdon\n        type tube. Include caption \"WATER\" on dial face.\n\n2.09    AUTOMATIC BALL DRIP\n\n   A.   Automatic Ball Drip shall be 3/4\" Potter-Roemer Fig. 5982 or Croker Corp. Fig. 6781.\n\n2.10    LADDERS\n\n   A.   Provide permanent heavy steel ladders to provide access to valves in accordance with\n        the code requirements. Ladders shall be of width and height required, shall be made of\n        heavy steel bars and heavy rungs and shall be permanently fastened at location. Where\n        the shut-off valve adjacent to the sprinkler alarm valve is located higher than 6' above\n        the floor, ladder shall be provided where directed.\n\n2.11    PAINTING\n\n  A.    Paints used on dedicated piping to combination sprinkler and standpipe shall not:\n        1.     Exceed the VOC content limits established in the Green Seal Standard GS-11\n               Paints, first edition, May 20, 1993.\n        2.     Exceed the VOC content limit of 250 g/L established in the Green Seal Standard\n               GC-03, Anti-Corrosive paints, second edition, January 7, 1997.\n\n  B.    Provide colors indicated in Paragraph 3.04\n        1.    First (1st) coat – Alkyd Vinyl Acrylic – Latex Primer – 1.2 Mills DFT\n        2.    Second (2nd) coat – Semi-Gloss Vinyl Acrylic Latex – Enamel – 1.3 Mills DFT\n\n2.12    VALVE SUPERVISORY SWITCHES\n\n  A.    Manufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\n        the following:\n        1.     Potter Electric Signal Co. Model OSYSU-2\n        2.     Fire-Lite Alarms, Inc.; a Honeywell company.\n        3.     Kennedy Valve; a division of McWane, Inc.\n        4.     System Sensor; a Honeywell company.\n\n  B.    Standard: UL 346.\n\n  C.    Type: Electrically supervised.\n\n  D.    Components: Single-pole, double-throw switch with normally closed contacts.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 6\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n  E.    Design: Signals that controlled valve is in other than fully open position.\n\n  F.    Locate on each valve as designated on the drawings. Switches shall be mounted so not\n        to interfere with the normal operation of the valve and shall be adjusted to operate\n        within two revolutions of the valve control or when the stem has moved no more than\n        one-fifth of the distance from its normal position. The switch mechanism shall be\n        contained in a weatherproof die-cast aluminum housing which shall provide 3/4” tapped\n        conduit entrance and incorporate the necessary facilities for attachment to the valve.\n        Switch housings shall be finished in red baked enamel.\n\n\nPART 3 - EXECUTION\n\n3.01    EXAMINATION\n\n   A.   Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Administrative\n        Requirements: Coordination and project conditions.\n\n  B.    Verify blocking in place for cabinet installation.\n\n3.02    INSTALLATION\n\n  A.    Install in accordance with NFPA 14.\n\n  B.    Install cabinets plumb and level. Secure to adjacent surfaces. Establish top of cabinet\n        (inside horizontal) surface 66 inches above finished floor.\n\n   C.   Install hose station valve in cabinet at 60 inches above floor.\n\n   D.    Connect standpipe system to water source separate from domestic water connection.\n\n   E.    Where static pressure exceeds 100 psi at any hose station, furnish pressure orifice disc\n         in discharge of hose station valve to prevent pressure on hose exceeding 90 psi.\n\n   F.    Install three-way fire department outlet on roof.\n\n3.03     FIELD QUALITY CONTROL\n\n   A.   Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Quality Requirements,\n        and Execution and Closeout Requirements: Field inspecting, testing, adjusting and\n        balancing.\n\n   B.    Test entire system in accordance with NFPA 14.\n\n   C.    Require test be witnessed by Fire Marshall, Authority having jurisdiction and Owner's\n         insurance underwriter.\n\n3.04     TESTING\n\n   A.   Hydrostatic Testing: After flushing system, test standpipe piping hydrostatically, for\n        period of 2 hour, at not less than 300 psi or 50 psi in excess of the system working\n        pressure, whichever is greater. Check system for leakage of joints. The test pressure\n        shall be read from a gage located at the low point of each system or zone being tested.\n        1.     Repair or replace piping system as required to eliminate leakage.\n\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 6                                           FIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building                                                21 12 00 - 7\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000              Issued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n        2.    Test the entire fire protection installation, including fire alarm system, in\n              accordance with the requirements of the NYC Fire Code and give at least 2 days\n              advance notice in writing of tests and inspections to the Construction Inspection\n              Division and the Authority. Tests shall be conducted in the presence of the any\n              public authority having jurisdiction. All tests shall be performed as part of this\n              contract.\n\n3.05    FIELD PAINTING\n\n  A.    Protect sprinkler heads during painting with small paper bags. Painting of sprinkler/ fire\n        standpipe piping, hangers, and all other items and accessories shall conform to the code\n        requirements.\n\n  B.    Paint standpipes in accordance with Specification Section 21 05 00.\n\n3.06    CLEANING\n\n   A.   Information for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\n        Requirements: Final cleaning.\n\n   B.   Flush entire system of foreign matter.\n\n\n                                                        END OF SECTION 21 12 00","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138611232}}
