{"type":"message","id":"225048ea","parentId":"5d545496","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:13:27.168Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Test Alpha is complete. Let me summarize the findings for the main agent.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"## Test Alpha Complete - Summary\n\n**Methodology:** Bid-Breakdown-First approach - started from 10 Fire Protection bid items (43-51, 95), routed to Fire Protection expert, extracted only targeted specs and drawings.\n\n### Key Findings\n\n**System Overview:**\n- 26-floor building (Cellar through Penthouse)\n- Combined Wet Standpipe and Sprinkler System (Class I/III)\n- **7 Standpipes** - 1 base scope + 6 as alternates\n- Fire Pump (2,155 lbs) + Jockey Pump (135 lbs) on Mezzanine\n- 4 Fire Department Connections (3\"x3\"x6\")\n\n**Piping:**\n- 10\" main from pump\n- 8\" main risers\n- 6\" floor risers\n- 4\" sprinkler FCAs\n- Estimated 4,000+ LF total\n\n**Major Cost Drivers:**\n1. Fire Pump assembly\n2. 7 Standpipes (6 alternates = separate pricing)\n3. 26-floor height requiring pressure zones/PRVs\n4. 4 FDCs (polished brass)\n5. Fire-rated hose cabinets per floor\n6. NYC/FDNY compliance\n\n**RFIs Identified (5):**\n1. Fire Pump GPM/HP ratings (need FP-002 schedule)\n2. Sprinkler head count not detailed\n3. Pipe LF detailed schedule needed\n4. Valve count by size needed\n5. Hydraulic calc responsibility\n\n**Metrics:**\n- Documents processed: 14\n- Spec sections analyzed: 3 (21 05 04, 21 05 05, 21 12 00)\n- Bid items analyzed: 10\n- Issues/RFIs found: 5\n- Coordination items: 5\n- Time: ~7 minutes\n\n**Confidence:** Medium-High\n- System understanding: High\n- Quantity accuracy: Medium (needs detailed drawing takeoff)\n\nResults written to: `test-alpha-results.json`"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":8,"output":523,"cacheRead":82460,"cacheWrite":839,"totalTokens":83830,"cost":{"input":0.00004,"output":0.013075,"cacheRead"